<section id="8120-intercollegiate-athletics-participation-responsibility-for-maintenance-director-of-athletics-and-recreation-anchor" class="flex-wrapper standard clearfix" >
<h2>8120 Intercollegiate Athletics Participation Responsibility for Maintenance: Director of Athletics and Recreation</h2>                    
<p><strong>I. Policy Statement</strong><br />
• The Athletics Department is committed to supporting the College’s mission by making a difference in the lives of student athletes. Athletics is an educational opportunity and experience that complements a student’s formal classroom education. Athletic participation helps to facilitate the development of young adults by teaching and reinforcing life skills. Collegiate athletics requires a special commitment and willingness to accept greater expectations and responsibilities. First and foremost, the College expects its student-athletes to be successful in the classroom. Additionally, student-athletes are expected to compete at the highest level while learning valuable life lessons by participating as part of a team and living, learning, and contributing to a diverse community. Participating in RBC athletics is a privilege, not a right.</p>
<p>• The College shall be recognized as having a nationally competitive athletics program dedicated to positively influencing the academic, personal, social, and athletic development of its student-athletes. The athletics program shall compete to win while teaching life lessons, reinforcing healthy behaviors, and providing opportunities to learn new skills and develop positive habits that collectively assist student-athletes in reaching their full potential.</p>
<p><strong>II. Reason for Policy</strong><br />
This policy clarifies the nature of intercollegiate athletics participation as a privilege, not a right, and describes behavioral expectations for student athletes. This policy is not intended, nor shall it be construed, to limit coaching staff discretion as to team membership, participation, playing time, and similar decisions, subject to compliance with the specific minimum standards set forth above.</p>
<p><strong>III. Applicability of the Policy</strong><br />
All Athletic Department staff, actual and prospective student-athletes, and Richard Bland College athletics boosters shall become familiar with this policy.</p>
<p><strong>IV. Related Documents</strong><br />
NJCAA Handbook/Casebook<br />
Clarification of Intercollegiate Athletics Policy Guidance: The Three-Part Test<br />
Office of Civil Rights &amp; Title IX Enforcing info from US Dept. of Ed</p>
<p><strong>V. Contacts</strong></p>
</section><!--.flex-wrapper-->
<section id="" class="flex-wrapper clearfix">
<table class="acf-table-editor"><tr><td>Office</td><td>Title</td><td>Telephone Number</td><td>Email</td></tr><tr><td>Athletics Department</td><td>Director of Athletics and Recreation</td><td>(804) 862-6250</td><td>office.athletics@rbc.edu</td></tr><tr class="row-to-hide"><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></table>        
</section><!--.flex-wrapper-->
<section id="" class="flex-wrapper standard clearfix" >
<p><strong>VI. Procedures</strong><br />
Student athletes and members of the RBC Athletic Department, when applicable, must comply with:</p>
<ul>
<li>Applicable federal, state, and local laws</li>
<li>Richard Bland College Student Conduct and Disciplinary Procedures</li>
<li>National Junior College Athletic Association (NJCAA) rules and regulations</li>
<li>Athletic Department procedures, rules, and regulations</li>
<li>Team rules and coaching instructions</li>
</ul>
<p>Each individual involved in intercollegiate athletics is obligated to know and act in full compliance with these requirements; and to report any violation of NJCAA, conference, and/or College policies or rules of which he or she is aware to his or her head coach or the Athletics Director.</p>
<p>If a student-athlete is involved in conduct that violates any or all of these requirements, he or she will be subject to appropriate disciplinary action to be determined at the discretion of the team’s Head Coach and/or the Athletic Director (or a designee). Such disciplinary action may include, without limitation, temporary or permanent revocation of athletic privileges, and is in addition to any other consequences that may apply pursuant to applicable laws and/or College policies, procedures, rules, and regulations.</p>
<p><em><u>Policy History<br />
</u></em><em>Approved November 20, 2015<br />
</em><em>Updated January 11, 2017</em></p>
<p>&nbsp;</p>
</section><!--.flex-wrapper-->
<section id="8130-adjunct-faculty-teaching-load-policy-anchor" class="flex-wrapper standard clearfix" >
<h2>8130 Adjunct Faculty Teaching Load Policy</h2>                    
<p class="p3"><b>Policy Number: 8130 Policy Name: </b><span class="s2"><b>Adjunct Faculty Teaching Load Policy </b></span><b>Responsible Office: Academics </b></p>
<p class="p3"><b>Effective Date: July 1, 2026 </b></p>
<p class="p3"><b>Last Updated: Initial </b></p>
<p class="p3">I. <b>Policy Statement </b>Adjunct faculty Richard Bland College (“RBC” or “College”) may be assigned no more than twelve (12) credit hours of credit-bearing instruction during the fall or spring semester.</p>
<p class="p3">Adjunct faculty may not exceed this limit through multiple appointments within the College. The credit-hour maximum applies to the total combined instructional load at RBC for a given semester.</p>
<p class="p3">Adjunct faculty are expected to disclose any additional teaching or instructional assignments at other institutions to their department chair prior to the start of each semester. Adjunct faculty should consider their total instructional load across all institutions and its potential impact on instructional quality, student availability, and course preparation.</p>
<p class="p5">II. <b>Reason for Policy </b>The reason for the policy is to establish a clear, consistent, and legally compliant limit on the instructional load of adjunct faculty at RBC. The policy affirms the College’s commitment to instructional quality, faculty wellbeing, compliance with federal and Commonwealth of Virginia workforce requirements, and the clear distinction between adjunct and full-time faculty roles.</p>
<p class="p5">III. <b>Applicability of the Policy </b>This policy is applicable to all adjunct faculty at RBC. Instructional assignments associated with dual enrollment courses taught under separate non-RBC contractual or school-division arrangements are excluded from this policy.</p>
<p class="p5">IV. <b>Responsibilities </b>The Department chairs are responsible for monitoring adjunct instructional assignments each semester. The Chief Academic Officer shall conduct periodic audits to ensure compliance with this policy.</p>
<p class="p3">V. <b>Contact </b></p>
</section><!--.flex-wrapper-->
